THIRD-PARTY FONT LICENSES

The MIT license above does NOT cover the bundled typeface data. Subsetting a
font and converting its outlines to path data creates a Modified Version under
the SIL Open Font License, which requires that the derived material stay under
that same license. The following files are therefore licensed under the terms
of the fonts they were derived from, not under MIT:

  fonts/**                       original typefaces, unmodified, with licenses
  src/core/fonts/monolith.ts     derived from Bowlby One    (OFL 1.1)
  src/core/fonts/archivo.ts      derived from Archivo Black (OFL 1.1)
  src/core/fonts/ultra.ts        derived from Ultra         (Apache 2.0)
  src/core/fonts/modak.ts        derived from Modak         (OFL 1.1)

The build output in dist/ embeds that derived data and carries the same
obligations when redistributed on its own.

  Bowlby One    Copyright (c) 2011 by vernon adams (vern@newtypography.co.uk),
                with Reserved Font Names "Bowlby", "Bowlby One" and
                "Bowlby One SC". SIL Open Font License 1.1 —
                full text in fonts/bowlby/OFL.txt.
                Because the grant reserves those names, the derived subset is
                presented to users as "Monolith".

  Archivo Black Copyright 2017 The Archivo Black Project Authors
                (https://github.com/Omnibus-Type/ArchivoBlack).
                SIL Open Font License 1.1 — fonts/archivo/OFL.txt.

  Ultra         Copyright (c) 2010 by Brian J. Bonislawsky DBA Astigmatic
                (AOETI). Apache License 2.0 — fonts/ultra/LICENSE.txt.
                Changes from the original are stated at the top of
                src/core/fonts/ultra.ts.

  Modak         Copyright (c) 2015 Ek Type (www.ektype.in).
                SIL Open Font License 1.1 — fonts/modak/OFL.txt.

Each generated glyph table repeats its own copyright, license and list of
changes in a header comment.
